  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: All 8 completed experiments are singleprofile with no aggregation. The best configuration (config_049: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 0.5353 acc, with PCA clearly dominating scgpt as RNA encoder and image adding ~5% over RNA-only. The largest unexplored design dimension is whether multiprofile + aggregation improves upon the single-profile baseline. Question: Does adding multiple profiles with average-pool aggregation improve over the best singleprofile setting, holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion (concat) constant? Why this experiment: config_048 is the minimal-change extension of config_049—only profile_setting and aggregation differ—so any performance delta cleanly isolates the multiprofile+aggregation effect. Starting with the simplest aggregation (avgpool) before transformer ensures we first learn whether multiprofile itself is beneficial before attributing gains to a more complex aggregation mechanism. This is the highest-information experiment available under the budget constraint."
}

